WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.460
Hey guys. How's it going? It's Justine.

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.380
Today we are going to be checking out some new

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:04.700
Nintendo Switch accessories.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.900
It's not a secret that I'm obsessed with my Nintendo Switch--

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.200
still--yes-- I'm still obsessed.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.260
I now, officially, have beat Zelda,

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.620
I ended up beating Gannon on the plane and it was

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.400
kind of awkward because I had no one to celebrate with.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.380
I really did want to wait until I was home to beat it but,

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.580
I basically had five hours to kill on the plane

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:21.780
and I thought "Now's the time".

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.900
Anyway, lets check these out and you guys can be

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.420
can be on your way onto the next video

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:26.640
after you're done watching this.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.740
The first thing I wanted to show you was...

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:29.780
This.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.600
This is a hand-made, leather, Nintendo Switch bag,

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.200
made in San Francisco,--

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.140
did I mention, "Hand-Made"--

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.580
The place is called: "Water Field"?

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.200
sfbags.com..

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.640
So someone tweeted me saying , "The Game Over Greggy

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.440
recommended this" and that I "should get it".

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:47.880
And then I went to take a look at the bags and I was like

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.360
"Wow, these are pretty awesome."

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:51.900
They have a bunch of different options and color combinations

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.880
but this was the one I went with because I feel like black is my favorite color.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.460
So its got this really nice, little zipper back here.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:58.640
Its a nice little mesh.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:01.500
So you can put, like, some cords, or--really whatever else

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.020
you want to put in here.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:03.900
I mean, I can actually put my phone in there,

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:04.800
or wallet.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.240
I mean, this could essentially be a purse.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:06.800
[Zips zipper]

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.620
Like, I don't want to stray guys away from getting this, but,

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:10.920
I mean, this is a nice clutch-

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:12.860
like this is, this looks good.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.660
They also give you some options of accessories

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:15.960
that you can get with it.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:17.620
And I am such a sucker for all of these clips

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:18.700
because I use these for everything.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.920
I clip them on my purse -- I use them when I walk the dog--

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:22.640
I love being able to hook tons of different things

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:23.480
on.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:24.600
So I think this was, um-

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:25.540
[Clip clatters]

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:26.900
[Shocked expression]

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.920
When you're at the checkout, it gives you the option

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.680
to add these onto your bag.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:32.820
So these were the different accessories that you could add on.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.480
You could add this clip, you could add the leather strap,

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.480
or this matte black clip-

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.360
I don't remember exactly what they were called but,

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.500
you'll see on the website if you decide to get this--

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.440
And this clips off just like so.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.140
So its got places to put your games right here,

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.020
which are very nice.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:50.720
Although, I plan on doing as many, all digital games as possible.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.040
So if you could see inside here, there's a bunch of different, little pockets as well.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:56.260
Put this in there,

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:58.340
fits,

00:01:58.860 --> 00:01:59.740
like a glove;

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:01.240
and it actually fits quite well.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.780
And its got these little...

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.760
magnetic buttons here..

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:05.660
[Snaps buttons]

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:07.460
This is a really good-lookin bag.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:10.400
And its nice and padded in here as well so,

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:10.900
I feel like,

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.900
even if you put this inside of another bag,

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:15.760
or... you do end up wearing it sort of as a

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:16.260
wristlet type thing,

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.080
it will have some padding and protection.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.440
Next up are these little...

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.000
What are these?

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:21.980
These are headphones.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:23.220
So, Nintendo sent me this,

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.040
the backpack and this case to check out.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.680
So, thank you Nintendo, I appreciate it

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:29.900
because I have definitely bought way too many

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:31.780
Nintendo accessories for the Switch.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:33.700
Let's check these out, these are

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.820
Zelda case and chat earbuds.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.220
[Rips open package]

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:38.520
Oh that's cute!

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:43.140
So this has, like, the little area to put your headphones in;

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.800
and you can wrap the cable around there to keep them

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:46.520
nice and neat.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.400
These  look pretty good!

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.580
Yeah, just pop that in there.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.460
Ok, I'm going to be completely honest with you,

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.640
this is taking too much time. [Chuckles]

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:00.740
I feel like I'm never gonna just...roll these up again.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.200
Sarcastically: "Wow!"

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:08.800
"Suuper official!"

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.240
Next up is this case,

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.240
my friend, Joy, actually had this one...

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:13.820
[Opening package]

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:16.440
I mean, if this doesn't say, "Hey! I got a Nintendo Switch in here!",

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:17.620
I don't know what does.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:20.480
I do think, I prefer, having a more subtle case.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.600
So if you're out and about, and somebody sees it, they're not, like,

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:24.880
"I'm stealing that. That's a Nintendo Switch in there."

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:26.280
[Rips more packaging]

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.900
So this has all kinds of accessories though.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:31.460
So these have some little bumpers that you can put on

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:32.460
your Joy-Cons.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.180
Talk about decked-out!

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.280
Got these little things that you can put on your

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:38.660
head-... well, I don't know what those are.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:39.280
[Click]

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.640
Wow. That snapped in pretty quick.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:45.380
I think that the blue might look a lot better on...

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.360
the grey Joy-Cons.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.440
Can you imagine having white Joy-Cons?

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:50.760
Absolutely beautiful!

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.040
[Unzips bag]

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:53.460
Let's take a look inside.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.140
Oh! It comes with a nice,

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.640
protective cover!

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.660
And--oh this is good because, the one that I put on,

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:01.880
I did a very terrible job and there's bubbles in it.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.300
So it looks like this just has a little velcro thing.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.160
Attach your Switch--

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:08.900
You definitely have a little bit of extra room there so,

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:10.040
be warned.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:12.280
I think that's one of the complaints that Joy had. She felt like

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:15.200
it didn't fit perfectly, where some of the other cases

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.580
do have a much tighter fit.

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:19.100
But, there is a lot more room in here for pretty much anything.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.060
Actually, you can probably put your Switch even in there.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:21.980
Yeah. This looks good.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:22.820
[Zips case]

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.440
Still not quite sure what these are fo--

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.940
Oh, I know what they--they're for this!!

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:30.240
They're the top of the [stammers "the"]...the controllers!!

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.960
I mean, that doesn't really look good in this color combination.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.020
I mean, if that's something your into...

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:37.000
go for it.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.400
Now that I have really been waiting for is

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.300
checking out this Nintendo Switch backpack.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:45.120
It even has a Nintendo Switch logo on it?

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:46.860
*sighs*

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.640
So on the front, we got this nice little zipper;

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.120
opens up quite nicely to have some more little...

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:58.820
zip places...to put things--zip places to put things-- what?

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:02.020
So inside the main zip pocket, it has two other zippered areas,

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:03.080
to put your items.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:05.780
Let's look inside.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:06.820
[Unzips backpack]

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.340
So here's one main, little pocket area--

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:10.960
I wonder if I can fit my laptop in here?

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.000
There's a lot of places to put things here.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:15.040
Oh, wow!

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.000
This is overwhelming.

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:22.420
There's also another zipper up here too to put stuff in.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:24.060
It's crazy. There is...

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:26.200
Wo-- there is so many pockets.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:29.140
Like, how many controllers do they think that we're gonna have?

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.040
There's one,

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:32.200
two,

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:33.320
three, four,

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:35.960
five, six-- there's like, six slots,

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:37.360
to put Joy-Cons in.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.680
It's quite nice right there.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:42.380
Put your Pro Controller there...

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:44.800
Joy-Con slot-- *whispering* they got so many!

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:46.720
So something that will be super important for me is:

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:48.400
will I be able to fit my laptop in it?

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:50.200
Let's see.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:51.660
I happen to have it sitting right here.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.660
Oh, yeah. I mean, there is so much room.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.840
Look at that. This is a 15 inch laptop.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:58.020
You can put it here,

00:05:58.380 --> 00:05:59.820
you can put it here--

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:01.540
There's a lot more room in this thing;

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:03.300
a lot more room than I thought.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:05.480
Also, really well made.

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:06.420
[Zips backpack]

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.000
The zippers: quite responsive;

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.000
Which is, a great quality in a zipper,

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.000
let me tell you

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.860
because, I have had some backpacks that I've bought

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:15.860
that were actually super expensive and I was like,

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:17.440
"This is a crap zipper!"

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:18.580
"What is this!?"

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:21.300
I have not a single complaint about this backpack.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:23.220
If you were gonna get any of the things that

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:23.860
I talked about today,

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:24.940
this is it.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:27.520
This would be my number one favorite.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.740
I actually like this backpack

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:31.040
way more than my um,

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:32.680
expensive, hand-made leather bag.

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:34.660
Mostly because I like to carry with me

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:36.640
absolutely everything.

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:37.760
And with this, I can.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:39.600
With this, it's basically

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:40.600
just my Switch,

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:42.540
some little accessories and things like that;

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:45.080
but, I mean, I can even put my Switch

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:46.740
in here,

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:49.000
then put it wherever I want.

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:51.780
This is nice.

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.560
Feel like this would be an everyday bag

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:54.880
and then maybe if I'm going to like,

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.440
a nice, fancy red carpet,

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:57.720
or, like, a party,

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.120
this would be my bag that I would take.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:02.640
[Transition]

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:04.780
So, to celebrate the launch of Mario Kart,

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:06.880
I'm actually going to play some Zelda right now,

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:08.280
but, after I play Zelda,

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:09.780
I'm going to play some Mario Kart.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:12.420
So this is kind of, like, a three-in-one video:

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:13.720
we've got an unboxing,

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:15.160
we've got Zelda gameplay,

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:15.980
and Mario Kart.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:18.160
So, what better way to celebrate, then,

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:19.440
then this?

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:22.000
And I really haven't been playing as much as I was

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:25.020
before, thankfully, because I was so obsessed and

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:26.740
disgusted with myself *Chuckles*.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.980
I was like: "You got to go outside,"

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:30.240
"you got to get videos done,"

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:31.740
"you got to get work done,"

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:33.020
"you can't just be sitting on the couch"

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:34.040
"doing nothing".

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:35.780
And, I wasn't doing nothing.

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:37.300
I was saving Hyrule.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:39.280
So, where am I now?

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:40.860
I don't remember where I left off.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.700
I still have a lot of shrines to get.

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:44.780
[Chuckles softly]

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:46.620
Sorry, horsies, I scared you.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:48.120
Did I scare you?!

00:07:51.640 --> 00:07:53.720
Is there any shrines over here?

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:55.940
There's gotta be something.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:58.580
Can you stop raining, please?

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:00.840
Is there anything special over here?

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:02.600
There's gotta be something over here.

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:04.600
Where's all the freakin' shrines at?

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:09.540
[Lightning strike]

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:11.240
Geez, oh my goodness!

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.500
Well, I'm just walking around a lot...

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:19.360
Get away! Get away! Get away!

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:20.280
Oh, god!

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:21.260
Ah!

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:23.960
Can it stop storming already?

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:25.440
I got stuff I got to climb.

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:27.500
Get away from me! Get away from it!

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:30.120
Get--stop it! Leave me be!

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:31.720
[Link slashes enemy]

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:33.340
Ooh, you're fierce.

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:36.780
[Link slashes enemy repeatedly]

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:39.860
*Sheepishly* My Guardian Sword is damaged?

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.060
Can you believe I just--I just died

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:46.560
like, trying to beat this piece of garbage guy?

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:48.120
You're fierce.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.780
I haven't died in this game in so long,

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:57.220
and that's how I go out?

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.100
That's how I go OUT!?

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:00.620
You're--

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.440
I was wasting my time anyway!

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:04.540
Ok, we're going somewhere else because,

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.200
clearly, this area sucks and I hate it.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:10.020
Ok, so where am I right now?

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:12.220
Oh!

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:15.020
Tarrey Town! I think I was supposed to do something...

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:18.480
Let's go check in and see how it's doing.

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:21.980
*whew*

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:23.640
That was so close.

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:26.620
This town is coming along

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:28.940
*singsongy* "niicely"

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:31.560
"Need homes"?

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:33.740
"20 bundles of wood"?

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:35.920
I think I have wood!

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:38.180
Do I not have enough wood? Shoot!

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:39.940
I don't have enough wood!

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:43.700
Ok, Mr.Man! I'll better bring you some wood.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:47.160
Yeah, I'll cut the trees down in my own town.

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:48.120
Cut--

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:48.700
[Chuckles slightly]

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:49.440
Cut it!

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:51.900
*Australian accent* "I need two more!"

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:53.820
*Regular accent* "Hey, why not use an axe, Justine"

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:55.760
Because, I'm an idiot.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:58.220
And, I don't think I have one.

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:01.520
I don't. I guess I'll just use my Master Sword.

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:02.340
Why not?

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:03.620
Wow!

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:05.820
That was a beastly hit!

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:07.460
Did I...

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:09.520
I did my math wrong.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:11.860
Shh.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:14.920
